Name a custom `target_json` spec file `<toolchain>.json`, not
`<toolchain>.target.json`.

rustc derives a JSON target's triple identity from the spec filename
with only the `.json` extension stripped, so `foo.target.json` yields
the triple `foo.target`. That stray `.target` then leaks into the
rustc triple, the sysroot directory (`lib/rustlib/foo.target/`) and
every diagnostic. Dropping the extra extension makes the triple equal
the `rust_toolchain` target name verbatim.

Only affects `target_json` toolchains (the `elif` branch); builtin
`target_triple` toolchains never reach this line.

--- a/rust/toolchain.bzl
+++ b/rust/toolchain.bzl
@@ -497,7 +497,7 @@
     elif ctx.attr.target_json:
         # Ensure the data provided is valid json
         target_json_content = json.decode(ctx.attr.target_json)
-        target_json = ctx.actions.declare_file("{}.target.json".format(ctx.label.name))
+        target_json = ctx.actions.declare_file("{}.json".format(ctx.label.name))

         ctx.actions.write(
             output = target_json,
